{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggtpUjN5wvXS44G7eVRc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dq ≈ 2140 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 760 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3490 cm⁻¹. The C value is unphysically large, so only Dq and B are reliable. I solved the d² Tanabe–Sugano matrices by hand and did not run any code.\n\n**Setup.** All energies are measured from the ³F barycentre. The ground state is ³T₁(F), which mixes with ³T₁(P).\n\n- The ³T₁ matrix is [[−6Dq, 4B], [4B, 15B]]. Its eigenvalues are E± = 7.5B − 3Dq ± √((3Dq + 7.5B)² + 16B²).\n- The ³T₂ energy is 2Dq.\n- The first transition is ν₁ = ³T₂ − ³T₁(1) = 5Dq − 7.5B + √((3Dq + 7.5B)² + 16B²).\n- The second transition is ν₂ = ³T₁(2) − ³T₁(1) = 2√((3Dq + 7.5B)² + 16B²).\n\n**Dq and B from the two spin-allowed bands.**\n\n1. ν₂ = 25 000 cm⁻¹ gives √((3Dq + 7.5B)² + 16B²) = 12 500 cm⁻¹.\n2. Putting this into ν₁ = 17 500 cm⁻¹ gives 5Dq − 7.5B = 5000, so Dq = 1000 + 1.5B.\n3. Substituting back gives (3000 + 12B)² + 16B² = 12 500².\n4. This reduces to B² + 450B − 920 312 = 0, so B ≈ 760 cm⁻¹ and Dq ≈ 2141 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 21 400 cm⁻¹).\n5. The ground-state energy is then E₋ ≈ −13 219 cm⁻¹.\n\n**C from the ¹E line.**\n\nThe ¹E state is a t₂² state that mixes with e² ¹E. Its matrix is [[−8Dq + 9B + 2C, 2√3 B], [2√3 B, 12Dq + 8B + 2C]]. I recalled the diagonal and off-diagonal terms from the d² Tanabe–Sugano matrices and checked them against the Dq = 0 limit. There they reproduce the ¹D and ¹G energies, 5B + 2C and 12B + 2C.\n\n1. The observed line puts ¹E at E₋ + 9748 = −3471 cm⁻¹.\n2. With the values above, the diagonal terms are −10 281 + 2C and 31 770 + 2C.\n3. The lower eigenvalue is −10 445 + 2C.\n4. Setting this equal to −3471 gives 2C ≈ 6975, so C ≈ 3490 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Caveat.** C/B ≈ 4.6 is high, since typical values are about 4. The ¹E energy is very sensitive to B and Dq, so the C value is poorly determined and probably unreliable.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2141, \"B\": 760, \"C\": 3490, \"out_of_